# PhoneLab environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and adjust.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: everything below is optional. With no .env at all, PhoneLab
# runs on the file-backed local driver, which is the intended `npm run dev`
# experience.
#
# PRODUCTION (including every Vercel deployment, preview ones too): the two
# Supabase variables are REQUIRED. PhoneLab refuses to start without them rather
# than falling back to the file driver — that driver writes under process.cwd(),
# which is read-only inside a Lambda, so it produced a 500 on every sign-up and
# would silently lose every account even where it could write. See
# src/server/db/config.ts.
#
# Check any deployment with GET /api/health.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment identity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public origin of this deployment, with no trailing slash.
#
# Set this in production. It is the base for the MCP connector URL, the OAuth
# issuer, and the resource identifier that access tokens are bound to (RFC 8707) —
# so if it is wrong, Claude's tokens will be rejected. Left unset, PhoneLab derives
# it from the request's forwarded host, which is fine locally.
# PHONELAB_BASE_URL=https://phonelab.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `local`    — JSON file under PHONELAB_DATA_DIR. Development only.
# `supabase` — Postgres. Requires the two variables below.
#
# Omit this and PhoneLab picks Supabase when both Supabase variables are present,
# and the local driver otherwise — but only outside production. In production, or
# anywhere VERCEL is set, "otherwise" is a startup error, not a fallback.
# PHONELAB_STORE=local

# Escape hatch: allows the file driver in production anyway. Only for a throwaway
# instance where losing every account between invocations is acceptable.
# PHONELAB_ALLOW_LOCAL_STORE=1

# Where the local driver keeps its data. Defaults to ./.phonelab-data
# PHONELAB_DATA_DIR=./.phonelab-data

# Postgres via Supabase. REQUIRED in production. The service-role key must never
# reach the browser: it is only read by server code, behind PhoneLab's own
# authorisation checks, and must never be put in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
#
# Paste carefully — a trailing newline or a wrapping pair of quotes is the most
# common way one of these arrives broken. PhoneLab trims and unquotes both, and
# treats a whitespace-only value as unset rather than as configured.
#
# After setting them, apply the migrations in order:
#   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql
#   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/migrations/0002_onboarding.sql
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here, and there should not be. PhoneLab does not
# call a model API: users connect it to Claude as a custom connector and use their
# own subscription. PhoneLab provides the tools; Claude decides when to call them.
